00:40:59.880 --> 00:41:01.600
We were in the same graduating class.
我们是同一届毕业的。

954
00:41:01.700 --> 00:41:03.240
We went to NYU together.
我们一起在纽约大学读书。

955
00:41:03.700 --> 00:41:05.900
I was in the drama school.
我在戏剧学院。

956
00:41:05.900 --> 00:41:10.040
I got a degree in acting and he was not in the drama school.
我拿的是表演学位，而他不在戏剧学院。

957
00:41:10.040 --> 00:41:11.940
He got a regular, useful degree.
他拿的是那种正经、有用的学位。

958
00:41:13.480 --> 00:41:14.980
And look, I knew he performed.
听着，我知道他会表演。

959
00:41:15.120 --> 00:41:17.560
He did UCB and he was so funny.
他参加过UCB（正直公民剧团），而且特别搞笑。

960
00:41:17.720 --> 00:41:18.760
He's an incredible performer.
他是一位了不起的表演者。

961
00:41:19.040 --> 00:41:22.140
But I had no idea he was a professional actor.
但我完全不知道他是个职业演员。

962
00:41:22.260 --> 00:41:23.820
This is the first time I've seen him since college.
这是我大学毕业后第一次见到他。

963
00:41:24.380 --> 00:41:26.160
I was like, Zach, what the hell are you doing here, man?
我当时就想，扎克，你到底在这儿干嘛呢，伙计？

964
00:41:26.580 --> 00:41:27.800
That was quite a shock for me.
那对我来说真是个不小的冲击。

965
00:41:27.860 --> 00:41:31.280
If you just imagine one of your friends popping into your job and being like, oh, I work here now.
试想一下，你有个朋友突然出现在你的工作场所，跟你说，哦，我现在在这儿上班。

966
00:41:32.500 --> 00:41:33.140
That's insane.
那简直太疯狂了。

967
00:41:33.340 --> 00:41:33.940
I know.
我知道。

968
00:41:34.240 --> 00:41:39.940
And also, you guys, again, this was a time before Instagram, before you knew what everyone's life was.
而且大家伙儿，再次强调，那是在Instagram出现之前，在你还没法随时掌握每个人生活动态的年代。

969
00:41:40.040 --> 00:41:40.380
Yeah.
没错。

970
00:41:40.740 --> 00:41:43.480
You could honestly be surprised by running into someone.
你真的可能会因为偶遇某人而感到惊喜。

971
00:41:43.800 --> 00:41:47.220
This is very similar to you walking over to Accounting and Oscar sitting there.
这就像你走到会计部，发现奥斯卡坐在那儿一样。

972
00:41:47.380 --> 00:41:47.980
A hundred percent.
百分之百是这样。

973
00:41:48.560 --> 00:41:51.020
Well, I love that we were his first acting job.
嗯，我很高兴我们是他第一份表演工作。

974
00:41:51.340 --> 00:41:55.840
I love that when he left us then, it was because he was going to be the lead in another show.
我很高兴他当时离开我们，是因为他要去另一部剧里担任主角。

975
00:41:56.060 --> 00:41:56.360
Yeah.
没错。

976
00:41:56.360 --> 00:42:01.360
And as you know, he went on to have pretty big roles on Veep and New Girl and Black-ish.
如你所知，他后来在《副总统》、《杰茜驾到》和《喜新不厌旧》里都有相当重要的角色。

977
00:42:02.700 --> 00:42:05.480
And in fact, Angela, we got a fan question.
事实上，安吉拉，我们收到一个粉丝提问。

978
00:42:05.660 --> 00:42:05.940
Okay.
好的。

979
00:42:06.560 --> 00:42:07.580
From Sierra E.
来自马里兰州银泉市的塞拉·E。

980
00:42:07.740 --> 00:42:09.980
in Silver Spring, Maryland, and Debra J.
和马萨诸塞州的黛布拉·J。

981
00:42:10.240 --> 00:42:16.280
in Massachusetts, can we please talk about the office's connections to New Girl?
能不能请我们聊聊《办公室》和《杰茜驾到》之间的联系？

982
00:42:16.280 --> 00:42:17.080
Oh, yeah.
哦，当然。

983
00:42:17.640 --> 00:42:22.440
Angela, Oscar, Kate, and Nelson Franklin have all been on both The Office and New Girl.
安吉拉、奥斯卡、凯特和尼尔森·富兰克林都出演过《办公室》和《杰茜驾到》。

984
00:42:22.960 --> 00:42:25.540
Angela, what was it like working on New Girl?
安吉拉，在《杰茜驾到》工作是什么感觉？

985
00:42:26.190 --> 00:42:27.960
It was such a blaSt.
那真是太棒了。

986
00:42:28.060 --> 00:42:29.440
I had a recurring role.
我有一个常驻角色。

987
00:42:29.580 --> 00:42:34.220
I was a school teacher where Zoe's character also taught the same school.
我演一名学校老师，佐伊的角色也在同一所学校教书。

988
00:42:34.820 --> 00:42:36.280
We had so many fun scenes.
我们有很多有趣的戏份。

989
00:42:36.440 --> 00:42:38.100
I also had some really great scenes with Damon.
我和达蒙也有一些非常棒的对手戏。

990
00:42:38.100 --> 00:42:41.080
And that cast was so fun.
那个剧组真的很有趣。

991
00:42:41.260 --> 00:42:49.080
And also, the writers, it really felt familiar to me, like The Office, where you would do a scene, you would get it scripted.
还有编剧们，这让我感觉很亲切，就像《办公室》一样，你拍一场戏，先按剧本演。

992
00:42:49.220 --> 00:42:51.620
Maybe if you had an idea, you could pitch it, you know?
如果你有想法，或许还可以提出来，你懂的？

993
00:42:51.780 --> 00:42:53.880
I loved every second of being on that show.
我享受在那部剧里的每一秒。

994
00:42:54.020 --> 00:42:55.360
It was just great fun.
真的非常开心。

995
00:42:55.360 --> 00:42:57.260
And I'm still in touch with some of the cast members.
而且我和剧组的一些成员至今仍有联系。

996
00:42:57.760 --> 00:42:59.860
Here's one memory, though, that sticks with me.
不过，有一段记忆让我印象深刻。

997
00:43:00.120 --> 00:43:02.600
And it's not from one of the regular cast members.
而且那不是来自任何一位常驻演员。

998
00:43:03.080 --> 00:43:04.780
I was leaving one day.
有一天我正要离开。

999
00:43:04.940 --> 00:43:06.300
I had worked a half day.
我那天只工作了半天。

1000
00:43:06.300 --> 00:43:10.780
Anyway, as I was leaving the soundstage, Josh Gad was walking in.
总之，当我离开摄影棚时，乔什·盖德正走进来。

1001
00:43:11.260 --> 00:43:13.260
He was doing a part as well.
他当时也在演一个角色。

1002
00:43:13.340 --> 00:43:15.080
And we met sort of in the parking lot.
我们在停车场碰巧遇到了。

1003
00:43:15.160 --> 00:43:16.320
And we were like, oh, my gosh, how are you?
我们当时就说，天哪，你怎么样？

1004
00:43:16.420 --> 00:43:17.160
And we chit-chatted.
然后我们闲聊了几句。

1005
00:43:17.200 --> 00:43:18.040
How are things going?
最近怎么样？

1006
00:43:19.200 --> 00:43:23.500
And he said, oh, I just got this really cool project I'm pretty excited about.
他说，哦，我刚接了一个很棒的项目，我很兴奋。

1007
00:43:23.900 --> 00:43:25.680
I'm going to be a snowman.
我要演一个雪人。

1008
00:43:25.760 --> 00:43:28.160
I'm going to be the voice of a snowman in a movie.
我要在一部电影里为雪人配音。

1009
00:43:28.240 --> 00:43:28.640
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1010
00:43:28.800 --> 00:43:30.100
It was frozen.
是《冰雪奇缘》。

1011
00:43:31.160 --> 00:43:32.980
And he had just gotten the job.
他当时刚拿到那份工作。

1012
00:43:32.980 --> 00:43:34.640
And he was talking to me about it.
他还在跟我说这件事。

1013
00:43:34.640 --> 00:43:37.240
And I was like, I remember thinking, oh, that's so cool.
我当时记得我在想，哦，那太酷了。

1014
00:43:37.400 --> 00:43:38.760
You know, that could be really cool.
你知道，那可能会非常棒。

1015
00:43:38.920 --> 00:43:39.960
And it's frozen.
就是《冰雪奇缘》。

1016
00:43:40.240 --> 00:43:41.020
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1017
00:43:41.020 --> 00:43:41.800
He's Olaf.
他是奥拉夫。

1018
00:43:42.000 --> 00:43:42.860
He's Olaf.
他是奥拉夫。

1019
00:43:43.620 --> 00:43:44.100
Wow.
哇。

1020
00:43:45.280 --> 00:43:45.760
Wow.
哇。

1021
00:43:46.220 --> 00:43:52.020
Well, now we're going to move into Michael's office where Angela Oscar and Phyllis are trying
好了，现在我们要转到迈克尔的办公室，安吉拉、奥斯卡和菲利斯正试图

1022
00:43:52.020 --> 00:43:53.660
to reason with Michael.
劝说迈克尔。

1023
00:43:53.840 --> 00:43:55.740
They're saying everyone knows it was Andy.
他们说大家都知道是安迪干的。

1024
00:43:55.740 --> 00:43:59.280
And everyone shouldn't have to suffer because of it.
而且大家不应该因为这件事而受苦。

1025
00:43:59.400 --> 00:44:02.040
And Michael just needs to say it was Andy.
迈克尔只需要说出是安迪干的就行了。

1026
00:44:02.400 --> 00:44:04.500
And you all are wearing pink and purple.
你们都穿着粉色和紫色的衣服。

1027
00:44:04.820 --> 00:44:11.760
It's like you had a club called Throw Andy Under the Bus, and the dress code is pink and
就像你们成立了一个叫“把安迪推出去背锅”的俱乐部，而且着装要求是粉色和

1028
00:44:11.760 --> 00:44:12.120
purple.
紫色。

1029
00:44:12.520 --> 00:44:12.580
Yeah.
是啊。

1030
00:44:13.540 --> 00:44:16.960
The next scene is between Dwight and Joe in the conference room.
下一场戏是德怀特和乔在会议室里的对手戏。

1031
00:44:17.120 --> 00:44:18.260
I love this scene.
我喜欢这场戏。

1032
00:44:18.260 --> 00:44:22.120
And it has one of my absolute favorite lines in the whole episode.
它有我整集里最喜欢的台词之一。

1033
00:44:22.660 --> 00:44:27.060
Dwight says, I don't want to waste your time, and I wouldn't dare waste mine.
德怀特说，我不想浪费你的时间，我也不敢浪费我的时间。

1034
00:44:27.440 --> 00:44:29.380
It's like one of my favorite lines.
这简直是我最喜欢的台词之一。

1035
00:44:29.580 --> 00:44:31.320
I like want to say that in a meeting.
我真想在开会的时候说这句话。

1036
00:44:31.560 --> 00:44:32.920
He says he didn't do it.
他说他没做那件事。

1037
00:44:32.980 --> 00:44:36.500
And he doesn't know who exactly did, but he has a list of people she should fire.
他不知道具体是谁做的，但他有一份名单，上面写着她应该解雇的人。

1038
00:44:36.740 --> 00:44:38.820
Well, we got a fan question from Mary M.
嗯，我们收到了来自加拿大玛丽·M的一位粉丝提问，

1039
00:44:38.920 --> 00:44:41.420
in Canada asking about that liSt.
问的就是那份名单。

1040
00:44:41.820 --> 00:44:43.460
Here is what Mary had to say.
以下是玛丽的问题。

1041
00:44:43.980 --> 00:44:46.780
Number one, whose handwriting do you think that is?
第一，你们觉得那是谁的笔迹？

1042
00:44:46.780 --> 00:44:47.540
Is it Rain's?
是雷恩的吗？

1043
00:44:47.640 --> 00:44:48.560
Is it Phil Shea's?
是菲尔·谢的吗？

1044
00:44:49.200 --> 00:44:53.120
Number two, what are the numbers that correspond to each name?
第二，每个名字对应的数字是什么意思？

1045
00:44:53.560 --> 00:44:54.880
Michael has a five.
迈克尔是五。

1046
00:44:55.080 --> 00:44:55.880
Jim has a one.
吉姆是一。

1047
00:44:56.020 --> 00:44:56.760
Creed has a four.
克里德是四。

1048
00:44:56.900 --> 00:44:57.620
What does this mean?
这代表什么？

1049
00:44:58.220 --> 00:45:01.500
And finally, what's up with the order of this list?
最后，这份名单的顺序是怎么回事？

1050
00:45:01.640 --> 00:45:02.920
